    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Clinique Vétérinaire des Jasmins, at 714 avenue Rhin et Danube in Vence, welcomes dogs, cats and small pets in a setting equipped with up-to-date technology (digital X-ray, ultrasound, full blood analysers), with CCTV in the hospitalisation area and a digital health record accessible online. Reviews are mixed: some praise a competent, attentive team, others find some products pricey (a collar at €54 versus €34 elsewhere) or mention a vet who wasn't very attentive on one visit. The clinic does not advertise a 24/7 emergency service.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>As with any clinic, a call before coming lets you check availability, especially outside regular hours or in an emergency.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: save the clinic's number in your phone as soon as you arrive in Vence, it can come in handy if something unexpected comes up.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The old town of Vence, perched in the hinterland above Nice, is just a few minutes from the clinic.</p>
